#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:875
msgid "11. The `while` loop"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:884
msgid "The block runs again and again **while the condition is true**. Before each iteration Python tests the condition; when it is false, the loop ends and the program continues after the block."
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/02-conditions-and-loops.md:888
msgid "Inside the block, something must change the condition - otherwise the loop never ends. (Or a `break` stops it, section 13.)"
msgstr ""

